<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Costura embeds the listed assemblies INTO Dwight.gha and removes their loose DLLs from the output, so
     none can clash with another plugin's copy in the Grasshopper Libraries folder.

     Markdig (ADR-045) and MSAGL (ADR-063) are the Phase-6 baseline: pure-managed, no transitive deps, proven.

     WP-2.5 adds the cross-plugin CLASH surface pulled in transitively by the GhJSON chain: Newtonsoft.Json
     (the classic Grasshopper cross-plugin clash), Humanizer, and the json-everything trio (Json.More,
     JsonPointer.Net, JsonSchema.Net) - all pure-managed. GhJSON (loose) resolves these through Costura's
     AppDomain.AssemblyResolve hook (installed by Dwight.gha's module initializer, before GhJSON first loads).
     Dwight then stops adding a loose Newtonsoft to the ecosystem, and its own code binds its embedded copy
     when nothing else loaded one first.

     DELIBERATELY left loose (WP-2.5 decision, recorded in the as-built): GhJSON.Core / GhJSON.Grasshopper -
     Dwight-specific (not a common cross-plugin clash) and a GH-INTEGRATION assembly whose Costura embedding
     is the fragile part that needs the Rhino host to verify (build-green cannot prove it); and
     System.Text.Json / System.Text.Encodings.Web - framework-adjacent, where embedding risks a runtime
     conflict with the shared-framework copy. Tharun runtime-verifies that GhJSON's diagnostic commands (Read
     Selection / Dump GhJSON) still round-trip after this. -->
<Weavers xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="FodyWeavers.xsd">
  <Costura>
    <IncludeAssemblies>
      Markdig
      Microsoft.Msagl
      Newtonsoft.Json
      Humanizer
      Json.More
      JsonPointer.Net
      JsonSchema.Net
    </IncludeAssemblies>
  </Costura>
</Weavers>
